---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { sitePath } from '../../lib/siteUrl';
import StatusPill from '../../components/StatusPill.astro';
---

<Layout title="Layer Effects" description="Non-destructive shadows, blurs, glows, glass, and procedural layer effects for editable vector, text, raster, and grouped content in Varve.">
  <div class="container-custom">
    <div class="feature-page">
      <nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
        <a href={sitePath('/features')}>Features</a> / Layer Effects
      </nav>

      <div class="eyebrow"><StatusPill status="available" /> <span>Non-destructive appearance</span></div>
      <h1>Effects that stay attached to the layer</h1>
      <p class="feature-intro">
        Add shadows, glows, blur, glass, chromatic aberration, or glitch without flattening the source. Varve keeps the effect stack editable across vector shapes, paths, text, groups, frames, tables, image-filled objects, and raster layers.
      </p>

      <section class="feature-section feature-section--highlight">
        <h2>One stack, honest order</h2>
        <p>
          Layer Effects execute through explicit stages: backdrop acquisition, content effects, appearance effects, then material highlights and final compositing. Move controls are stage-aware, so every enabled reorder changes a meaningful within-stage order; a control never pretends that a cross-stage move changes the renderer.
        </p>
        <div class="stage-grid" aria-label="Layer Effects execution stages">
          <article><span class="stage-number">01</span><h3>Backdrop</h3><p>Background Blur and Glass Material sample the content behind the layer.</p></article>
          <article><span class="stage-number">02</span><h3>Content</h3><p>Gaussian, Layer, Field, Iris, Tilt-Shift, Path, Spin, Depth Blur, Chromatic Aberration, and Glitch transform painted content.</p></article>
          <article><span class="stage-number">03</span><h3>Appearance</h3><p>Shadows and glows wrap the authored source with stable, reorderable identity.</p></article>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="feature-section">
        <h2>Coverage that follows the pixels</h2>
        <p>
          Text effects follow shaped glyphs, counters, decorations, and strokes—not the invisible text box. Raster and image effects follow true alpha, transparent holes, crop placement, sparse tiles, and background-removal masks, so a cut-out PNG does not receive a rectangular shadow. Compound vector paths preserve curves, fill rules, and authored holes; gradients, translucent fills, and stroke-only content use painted coverage when a geometric outline would be misleading.
        </p>
        <div class="coverage-grid">
          <article><h3>Editable text</h3><p>Keep the font, rich formatting, transforms, and text content editable while shadows and glows follow the glyphs.</p></article>
          <article><h3>Raster layers</h3><p>Apply appearance effects to sparse tile surfaces without rerunning or replacing the original pixels.</p></article>
          <article><h3>Groups and frames</h3><p>Apply one composited-child silhouette at the container owner, preserving child ownership, clipping, and transparent gaps.</p></article>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="feature-section feature-section--highlight">
        <h2>Controls that match the effect</h2>
        <p>
          Each effect has its own vocabulary instead of inheriting a one-size-fits-all panel. Tune the things that define the look, then keep the source editable.
        </p>
        <div class="control-grid">
          <article><h3>Shadows and glows</h3><p>Shadows expose X/Y plus synchronized angle and distance. Glows add choke, contour, edge/center origin, and solid or effect-domain gradient colour treatment.</p></article>
          <article><h3>Chromatic aberration</h3><p>RGB split includes Mix and fractional offsets; Custom Color Split adds independent red, green, blue, luminance, or alpha contributions with output colours, strength, and offsets.</p></article>
          <article><h3>Glitch</h3><p>Direction, seed, density, slices, blocks, channel shifts, noise, scanlines, and blend mode.</p></article>
          <article><h3>Glass and depth</h3><p>Tint, saturation, brightness, noise, edge highlight, focus range, falloff, and depth inversion.</p></article>
          <article><h3>Spatial blur family</h3><p>Gaussian stays uniform; Field, Iris, Tilt-Shift, Path, and Spin expose their authored geometry and deterministic CPU reference rendering.</p></article>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="feature-section">
        <h2>Layer types at a glance</h2>
        <div class="support-table-wrap">
          <table class="support-table">
            <thead><tr><th scope="col">Owner</th><th scope="col">Supported</th><th scope="col">Effect source</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><th scope="row">Shapes and paths</th><td>Yes</td><td>Vector fills and strokes</td></tr>
              <tr><th scope="row">Text</th><td>Yes</td><td>Shaped glyph alpha</td></tr>
              <tr><th scope="row">Image-filled vectors</th><td>Yes</td><td>Placed image alpha and masks</td></tr>
              <tr><th scope="row">Raster layers</th><td>Yes</td><td>Tile surface alpha</td></tr>
              <tr><th scope="row">Groups and frames</th><td>Yes</td><td>Composited child surface</td></tr>
              <tr><th scope="row">Adjustment layers</th><td>Separate</td><td>Adjustment scope, not a drawable silhouette</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="feature-section">
        <h2>Everyday controls, without destructive surprises</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Add, edit, bypass, duplicate, reset, remove, and reorder effects with one-step history. Depth Blur enters through its image workflow so an effect is never saved without a valid DepthMap.</li>
          <li>Stable effect IDs keep masks attached through reorder, reset, duplication, transfer, save, and reload.</li>
          <li>Positive and negative spread use alpha expansion/contraction; spread is not disguised extra blur.</li>
          <li>Transparent backgrounds, compound paths, vector holes, text counters, and sparse raster pixels remain transparent instead of receiving a bounding-box effect.</li>
          <li>Mixed selections show missing rows and match compatible effects by identity before legacy stage/type order.</li>
          <li>Copying a stack deep-clones effect parameters and mints independent IDs for each destination.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="feature-section">
        <h2>Blur Gallery vocabulary, with Varve semantics</h2>
        <p>
          Gaussian, Field, Iris, Tilt-Shift, Path, and Spin Blur are editable effect-stack entries rather than destructive filters. Their controls use owner-local geometry, source-pixel blur distances, stable control IDs, and a linear-light premultiplied CPU reference so a saved document keeps the same meaning across Canvas2D fallbacks and reopen.
        </p>
        <p class="feature-note">Field pins, Iris regions, Tilt-Shift bands, Path points, and Spin pivots can be edited directly on the canvas or from the Inspector. The current CPU reference keeps the saved result deterministic; adaptive motion quality, bokeh, and restored grain remain deliberately scoped follow-ups.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="feature-section">
        <h2>Export with clear boundaries</h2>
        <p>
          The document stores the complete editable effect definition. When SVG, PDF, or another target cannot reproduce a backdrop, alpha, mask, blur, or procedural effect, Varve rasterizes the smallest affected compositing region rather than flattening the whole document. Vector geometry, text, and source assets remain editable in the document.
        </p>
        <p class="feature-note">Browser Canvas2D is the current pixel authority for this effect family; native interchange preserves the contract even where a target backend uses software replay.</p>
      </section>

      <div class="feature-cta">
        <h2>Build depth without losing editability</h2>
        <a href={sitePath('/download')} class="btn-default">Download Varve</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>

<style>
  .feature-page { max-width: 800px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 3rem 0; }
  .breadcrumb { font-size: .875rem; margin-bottom: 1.5rem; }
  .breadcrumb a { color: var(--text-secondary); }
  .eyebrow { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: .65rem; color: var(--text-secondary); font-size: .9rem; margin-bottom: 1rem; }
  .feature-page h1 { font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 2.7rem); font-family: var(--font-editorial); font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: -.02em; margin-bottom: 1rem; color: var(--text-primary); }
  .feature-intro { font-size: 1.25rem; color: var(--text-secondary); margin-bottom: 3rem; }
  .feature-section { margin: 3rem 0; }
  .feature-section--highlight { padding: 1.5rem; border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); border-radius: 1rem; background: var(--surface-card); }
  .feature-section h2 { font-size: 1.5rem; margin-bottom: 1rem; color: var(--text-primary); }
  .feature-section h3 { font-size: 1rem; margin: .5rem 0; color: var(--text-primary); }
  .feature-section p, .feature-section li { color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.7; }
  .stage-grid, .coverage-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: 1rem; margin-top: 1.5rem; }
  .control-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); gap: 1rem; margin-top: 1.5rem; }
  .coverage-grid article, .stage-grid article, .control-grid article { padding: 1rem; border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); border-radius: .75rem; }
  .stage-number { color: var(--accent-primary); font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; font-size: .8rem; }
  .support-table-wrap { overflow-x: auto; border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); border-radius: .75rem; }
  .support-table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; min-width: 560px; }
  .support-table th, .support-table td { text-align: left; padding: .8rem 1rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); color: var(--text-secondary); }
  .support-table thead th { color: var(--text-primary); font-size: .85rem; }
  .support-table tbody th { color: var(--text-primary); font-weight: 600; }
  .support-table tr:last-child th, .support-table tr:last-child td { border-bottom: 0; }
  .feature-section ul { padding-left: 1.3rem; }
  .feature-note { font-size: .9rem; }
  .feature-cta { margin-top: 4rem; padding-top: 2rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); text-align: center; }
  .feature-cta h2 { margin-bottom: 1rem; }
  @media (max-width: 700px) { .stage-grid, .coverage-grid, .control-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } .feature-page { padding: 2rem 0; } }
</style>
